config BP
    tristate "bp: ARM64 breakpoint driver (HWBP/PTEBP/STEPBP)"
    default m
    help
      ARM64 breakpoint driver providing three families through a stable
      ioctl ABI on /dev/bp:
        - PTEBP: PTE UXN execute breakpoints with in-kernel instruction
          emulation and S0 write-back on precise hits.
        - HWBP:  hardware breakpoints/watchpoints with per-register
          2-bit masks and hit records.
        - STEPBP: single-step PC breakpoints with generation tracking.
      Build with: make -C <KDIR> M=$PWD/bp/kernel ARCH=arm64 LLVM=1 modules
